ABSTRACT_EN = [
    ("p", "This project studies joint dynamic channel assignment and routing in multi-hop Wi-Fi mesh networks. We propose EGAT-MAPPO, in which every node is an agent that chooses its downlink channel and its parent. The model combines an edge-aware graph attention encoder (GATv2), GRU memory, two decision timescales and a residual prior from Ko's local-cost rule. It is warm-started by behaviour cloning from Ko, trained with MAPPO, and executed in a decentralised way with switch hysteresis that suppresses unnecessary switches."),
    ("p", "We evaluate it in a custom Python simulator with an 802.11ax PHY and ns-3 default path loss: 20 nodes, two gateways and six downlink channels, across 11 scenarios. The baselines are a static assignment (M0), Ko, Q-neutral, Yuan (GAT+DQN) and Li (GAT-A2C). Every learned method is trained with five seeds and tested on 20 topologies per scenario. We use a pre-registered five-metric composite and intervals that count the training-seed variance of both methods."),
    ("p", "The simulator's airtime model is calibrated against packet-level ns-3 (7.4% rms error) before training. In the main setting on the test topologies, EGAT-MAPPO's composite exceeds every adapted published baseline by more than 10% (Ko +21.9%, Li +13.7%, Yuan +19.1%), and all four pre-registered criteria are met on the test topologies, on fresh topologies never used for any decision (Ko +23.8%), and with queue-preserving switches. Most of the gain over Ko comes from fewer switches (52 versus 616 per episode); throughput rises 8.5%. When Li and Yuan receive the same hysteresis, EGAT-MAPPO still beats Li with hysteresis significantly (+5.7%, +10.7% on fresh topologies) but ties Yuan with hysteresis (+0.7%, interval spans zero). In ns-3 on three scenarios it significantly beats Li, Yuan, Li with hysteresis and M0, improves on Ko by 10.7% without significance, and ties Yuan with hysteresis."),
    ("p", "Keywords:  Channel assignment,  Routing,  Wi-Fi mesh,  Graph attention network,  MAPPO,  Multi-agent reinforcement learning"),
]

